# Volt Trades — Product Spec Memory

Source: `Volt_Trades_Website_Development_Specification.pdf` (v1.0, July 2026).
Also align with `CLAUDE.md`. Prefer this product model over generic fintech templates.

## Core concept

**LEARN. INVEST. BUILD.**  
Positioning: Learn Forex · Manage Capital · Explore Opportunities · Build the Future.

Build a **scalable ecosystem**, not a single-page investment website. Modules are connected but independently manageable.

## Two surfaces

1. **Public website** — Home, Learn, Trading Floor, Projects, Volt Society, About, Blog, Contact, legal, Login/Register.
2. **Authenticated platform** — Dashboard (overview, learn, invest, wallet/accounts, projects, society, notifications, support, settings).

Every public CTA must have a real destination. No dead buttons.

## Core modules

- **Forex Academy** — courses, lessons, quizzes, progress, certificates; free/paid/coupon/access control.
- **Trading Floor** — admin-configurable opportunities/packages (amount, duration, risk, terms, projection).
- **Wallet / Accounts** — deposit, course pay, invest, withdraw, transactions; balance from ledger only.
- **Projects** — roadmap/showcase (Shop, Community, Technology, Education, Events, Future Ventures).
- **Volt Society** — community mission/values + join/waitlist.
- **Payments** — gateway abstraction; course / deposit / investment / withdrawal (+ shop later).
- **Admin + RBAC** — users, KYC, courses, opportunities, investments, payments, projects, coupons, support, reports, audit, settings.

## Stack (locked)

Monorepo: `apps/web` (Next.js) + `apps/api` (NestJS/Fastify modular monolith) + `packages/*`. PostgreSQL + Prisma. S3-compatible object storage. No microservices. Redis only when a real queue/job need exists.
